<article class="env-lemma" id="08TE">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/08TE">Lemma <span data-tag="08TE">17.28.7</span>.</a> Let $X$ be a topological space. Let $\mathcal{O}_1 \to \mathcal{O}_2$ be a homomorphism of sheaves of rings on $X$. Let $x \in X$. Then we have $\Omega _{\mathcal{O}_2/\mathcal{O}_1, x} = \Omega _{\mathcal{O}_{2, x}/\mathcal{O}_{1, x}}$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This is a special case of Lemma <a href="/tag/08RR" data-tag="08RR">17.28.6</a> for the inclusion map $\{ x\}  \to X$. An alternative proof is to use Lemma <a href="/tag/08TD" data-tag="08TD">17.28.4</a>, Sheaves, Lemma <a href="/tag/007Z" data-tag="007Z">6.17.2</a>, and Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/031G" data-tag="031G">10.131.5</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>